{title: Above All (FJ_97_en)}
{song_number: 97}
{language: en}
{artist: Lenny LeBlanc; Paul Baloche}
{tempo: 64}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[A]Above all [E]powers, above all [A]kings,
[A]above all [E]nature and all created [A]things,
above all [F#m]wisdom and all the ways of [E]man,
[D]You were here before the world be[E]gan.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Crucified, [Bm7]laid behind the [E]stone;
You lived to [A]die, re[Bm7]jected and a[E]lone.
Like a [A]rose trampled on the [F#m]ground,
[D]You took the fall and [Bm7]thought of me, [Esus4]above [E]all. [A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[A]Above all [E]kingdoms, above all [A]thrones,
[A]above all [E]wonders the world has ever [A]known,
above all [F#m]wealth and treasures of the [E]earth,
[D]there's no way to measure what You're [E]worth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Crucified, [Bm7]laid behind the [E]stone;
You lived to [A]die, re[Bm7]jected and a[E]lone.
Like a [A]rose trampled on the [F#m]ground,
[D]You took the fall and [Bm7]thought of me, [Esus4]above [E]all. [A]
{end_of_chorus}
